CHAPTER VIII
SPECIAL PROTECTION OF CHILDREN
Article 15
(1) Special protection of children is provided to:
a. children in emergency situations;
b. children in conflict with the law;
c. children from minority and isolated groups;
d. children who are exploited economically and/or sexually;
e. children who are victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic substances, and other addictive substances abuse;
f. children who are victims of pornography;
g. children with HIV/AIDS;
h. children victims of abduction, sale, and/or trafficking;
i. children victims of physical and/or psychological violence;
j. children victims of sexual crimes;
k. children victims of terrorist networks;
l. children with disabilities;
m. children victims of maltreatment and neglect;
n. children with deviant social behavior; and
o. children who are victims of stigmatization from labeling related to their parents' condition.
(2) The Regional Government in implementing the handling of special protection of children as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 7
Child victims of acts of violence, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 6, also obtain the following special rights:
a. the right to respect and full utilization for survival, growth, and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and
e. the right to obtain freedom.

CHAPTER III
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 3
Protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination is organized based on the principles of:
a. respect for human rights;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. victim protection;
e. empowerment; and
f. integration.

CHAPTER XIV
FINANCING
Article 34
Financing for the implementation of protection of women's and children's rights from acts of violence is sourced from:
a. State Revenue and Expenditure Budget;
b. Provincial Regional Revenue and Expenditure Budget;
c. Regional Revenue and Expenditure Budget (APBD);
d. Village Revenue and Expenditure Budget; and
e. Other legal and non-binding financial sources in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

