c. provision of facilities;
d. monitoring; and
e. evaluation.
(3) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2), in the framework of realizing the objectives of protection of the rights of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with minimum service standards implemented by OPD/related agencies and the community.

Article 7
Child victims of acts of violence, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 6, also obtain the following special rights:
a. the right to respect and full utilization for survival, growth, and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and
e. the right to obtain freedom.

Article 16
The provision of services to victims is implemented with the principles of:
a. swift;
b. safe and comfortable;
c. sense of empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. easily accessible;
f. not subject to fees; and
g. guaranteed confidentiality.

